      "heading": "Smells, Mould, and the Drain",
      "html": "<p>The evaporator is cold and damp by design, and a damp, dark heater box is a good home for mould. A musty smell when the air conditioning first starts, especially after the car has sat, often means growth on the evaporator or a blocked condensation drain that has left water standing in the box. The drain tube under the car should drip clear water when the A/C runs; if it does not, and water appears inside the cabin, the drain is blocked.</p>\n<p>Cleaning the evaporator and clearing the drain fixes the smell at its source. Spraying a freshener into the vents only masks it. A filter that is changed on time also helps, because it keeps the leaves and debris that feed growth out of the box in the first place.</p>\n"
